# Example ReRDMFT input file: carbon monoxide, using the cc-pVDZ basis
# (downloaded from https://www.basissetexchange.org/), which includes D
# shells for both atoms (see co-cc-pvdz.gbs). Small enough (nLarge=30,
# nSmall=136) to actually build the RKB two-electron Coulomb repulsion
# tensor (C4_SPINOR) without CHOLESKY: it is built in slabs from the 8-fold
# packed (SS|SS) integrals and stored as unique elements only (52.7 million of
# the 207 million complex values, Utils/SymmetricEri.h; the rest is rebuilt by
# symmetry) -- no dense n^4 array is formed. Measured on the current build:
# ~2.1 minutes and ~3.6 GB peak RSS without DEBUG; this input runs with
# DEBUG TRUE, which builds dense tensors on demand for its validation suites:
# ~2.7 minutes, ~5.4 GB peak. For a lighter 4-component run of the same molecule
# see co_ccpvdz_c4_gnof_neo_cholesky.inp (CHOLESKY TRUE, ~0.9 GB).
# co-cc-pvtz.inp's cc-pVTZ basis (nLarge=70, nSmall=224) is far larger: an
# estimate of ~82 GB of peak memory was made for the earlier (exchange-symmetry
# only) storage and has not been re-measured with the current scheme.
NELEC 14
BASIS co-cc-pvdz.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
DEBUG TRUE

GEOMETRY
C   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   0.000000   0.000000   1.128000
END
